# The ledger of `big`: what Go's `math/big` (Go 1.27) and Python's `int`,
# `decimal` and `fractions` (3.15), with the functions of `math` and the
# built-ins Python reads integers of any size with, let a program do, one block
# per capability, and what Rebel answers. Go's `big.Float` is a binary float of
# chosen precision, not a decimal: its one block is refused below, and its
# rounding modes stand with the decimal's. Rust's standard library has no
# integer of any size, no decimal and no fraction, so its line is `-` in every
# block. The lists are this machine's, 2026-11-16: `go doc -all math/big`,
# `dir(int)`, `dir(decimal)`, `dir(decimal.Decimal)`, `dir(decimal.Context)`,
# `dir(fractions.Fraction)`.

capability integer/value  an integer of any size, held exactly, compared with `==`
  heroes  big.Integer, big.from_int
  go      big.Int, big.NewInt, Int.Set, Int.SetInt64, Int.IsInt64
  rust    -
  python  int, int.__new__
  note    one value has one form, so `==` compares values and an integer may key a map, as Python's int; Go compares with Cmp, its `==` comparing pointers

capability integer/from-int  an integer made from the language's own
  heroes  big.from_int, big.from_u64
  go      big.NewInt, Int.SetInt64, Int.SetUint64
  rust    -
  python  int(i)
  note    -

capability integer/to-int  an integer as the language's `i64` or `u64`, failing where it does not fit
  heroes  big.int_of, big.u64_of
  go      Int.Int64, Int.IsInt64, Int.Uint64, Int.IsUint64
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    Go's Int64 and Uint64 answer the low bits of a number past 64 bits and say nothing; here it fails `does_not_fit`, as IsInt64 would have told

capability integer/float  an integer as the nearest `f64`, and a float's integer part as an integer
  heroes  big.float_of, big.from_float
  go      Int.Float64, Float.Int
  rust    -
  python  float(int), int.__float__, int(float)
  note    the nearest float, ties to even, as Go's Float64 and Python's float answer; past the largest float Python raises OverflowError and Go answers an infinity, as here and as the language's `to_f64`; from a float, NaN fails `invalid` and an infinity `does_not_fit`, Python's ValueError and OverflowError

capability integer/parse  an integer read from text in base ten
  heroes  big.parse
  go      Int.SetString (base 10), Int.UnmarshalText, Int.UnmarshalJSON, Int.Scan
  rust    -
  python  int(str)
  note    a sign, `+` included, and digits; Python's spaces around the number and `_` between digits are `invalid`, as in Go and in `numbers.parse_int`

capability integer/parse-base  an integer read from text in a given base
  heroes  big.parse_base
  go      Int.SetString (base 2 to 62), big.MaxBase
  rust    -
  python  int(str, base)
  note    bases 2 to 62 as Go reads them, either case up to 36; Python stops at 36 and reads a prefix that matches the base (`int("0x1f", 16)`), here `invalid` as in Go

capability integer/parse-literal  an integer read with its base told by its prefix
  heroes  big.parse_literal
  go      Int.SetString (base 0)
  rust    -
  python  int(str, 0)
  note    the language's own spelling, as `numbers.parse_int_literal` reads it: Go's and Python's base 0 also read `0X1F` and `0x_ff`, and Go a lone leading zero as octal

capability integer/format  an integer written in base ten
  heroes  big.format
  go      Int.String, Int.MarshalText, Int.MarshalJSON, Int.Append, Int.AppendText
  rust    -
  python  str(int), int.__str__, int.__repr__, int.__format__ ("d")
  note    -

capability integer/format-base  an integer written in a given base
  heroes  big.format_base
  go      Int.Text, Int.Format ("b", "o", "x", "X")
  rust    -
  python  bin, oct, hex, int.__format__ ("b", "o", "x", "X")
  note    no prefix and lower case letters, as Go's Text; Python's bin, oct and hex write `0b`, `0o`, `0x`; upper case is `strings.to_upper` of the text

capability integer/bytes  an integer read from bytes and written as bytes, either order, signed or not
  heroes  big.from_bytes, big.from_bytes_signed, big.to_bytes, big.to_bytes_signed, big.to_bytes_width, big.to_bytes_signed_width, big.ByteOrder
  go      Int.SetBytes, Int.Bytes, Int.FillBytes
  rust    -
  python  int.from_bytes, int.to_bytes
